---
const { portrait } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="grid grid-cols-[300px_1fr] border-b border-rule max-md:grid-cols-1">
  <div class="flex flex-col border-r border-rule py-8 pl-10 pr-8">
    <div class="flex min-h-[200px] flex-1 items-end border border-rule-strong bg-paper-2 p-3">
      {portrait ? <img src={portrait} alt="Brynn Caputo" class="h-full w-full object-cover" /> : <span class="label text-[10px]">portrait</span>}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="px-10 pb-8 pt-[34px]">
    <div class="label mb-3.5 text-blue">Who's building this</div>
    <h3 class="max-w-[44ch] text-[22px] font-semibold leading-[1.25] -tracking-[0.015em] text-balance">Twenty years making software make sense — and lately, things you can stand inside.</h3>
    <p class="mt-3.5 max-w-[68ch] text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-2 text-pretty">
      I'm Brynn. I design products for teams who need the thing to actually work — loyalty apps at Perka and Clover, claims tooling in healthcare, an audit system at Side that tripled auditor throughput. Between those I build installations, characters, and hackable terminals for desert festivals. Same instinct, different materials.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-[22px] flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-7 border-t border-rule pt-4 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.06em] text-ink-3">
      <span><span class="uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-4">Clients</span> &nbsp;Clover · Perka · Side · Sony · Habitat</span>
      <span><span class="uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-4">Shown at</span> &nbsp;The New Frame · Neotropolis · Wasteland</span>
      <a href="/about" class="border-b border-blue pb-0.5 uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-blue">More about me →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
